The core recommendation is to proceed with the development of this platform as a prototype for a national-scale research intelligence infrastructure. This framing is critical to securing stakeholder buy-in and achieving the desired strategic outcomes. The project is not merely an internal tool; it is a tangible contribution to India's national AI mission, embodying the shift towards sovereign, data-centric AI systems built on Indian data and principles [[7,15]]. By successfully implementing this vision, IIT Gandhinagar can establish itself as a premier hub for secure AI innovation, a reputation significantly bolstered by the institute's existing activities, such as organizing 'AI Day' events focused on responsible AI adoption and translational research pathways [[14]].

